The statute's retention rule states that records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute [[cite:obs-133ebd6cbb174d35689c945c2cf994b702117907 "Records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute."]]. The records are kept for eleven calendar years, after which they are shredded [[cite:obs-b5caf199d369505261c98ceb2581dbb9eafab40c "Ledgers: eleven calendar years, shredding afterwards."]].